<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carta de Logu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1392">1392</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Carta de Logu of Arborea</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Carta de Logu is a law code issued in the Sardinian language by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eleanor-of-arborea">Eleanor of Arborea</a> in 1392, revising an earlier code of her father Marianus IV. It covered civil and criminal law, rural life and the rights of women. After the Aragonese conquest of Arborea it was extended to most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> and remained in force until 1827.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carta-de-logu.jpg" alt="Carta de Logu" width="320" height="456" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Harlok83 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pag1_carta_delogu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
